  "issue": {
    "body": "HTTP spec allows multiple headers of the same key to be present. This is why libraries such as h11 accept a list of headers instead of dictionaries. \r\n\r\n[HTTP 1.1, section 4.2](http://www.w3.org/Protocols/rfc2616/rfc2616-sec4.html#sec4.2)\r\n\r\nCurrently starlette dosen't support this because it is just running `value.encode()` on the value in the header. \r\n\r\nI propose that the header dictionary be able to contain lists as values as well, in which case starlette will add a header for each value. \r\nThis is most common when using the `set-cookie` header, when a backend wants to add multiple cookies, but not have the one header exceed too big of an individual header length. \r\n\r\nfor example:\r\n```\r\nheaders = {'mykey': ['value1', 'value2']}\r\n```\r\n\r\nwould produce the following headers:\r\n\r\n```\r\nmykey: value1\r\nmykey: value2\r\n```\r\n\r\n\n\n<!-- POLAR PLEDGE BADGE START -->\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> - We're using [Polar.sh](https://polar.sh/encode) so you can upvote and help fund this issue.\n> - We receive the funding once the issue is completed & confirmed by you.\n> - Thank you in advance for helping prioritize & fund our backlog.\n\n<a href=\"https://polar.sh/encode/starlette/issues/650\">\n<picture>\n  <source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://polar.sh/api/github/encode/starlette/issues/650/pledge.svg?darkmode=1\">\n  <img alt=\"Fund with Polar\" src=\"https://polar.sh/api/github/encode/starlette/issues/650/pledge.svg\">\n</picture>\n</a>\n<!-- POLAR PLEDGE BADGE END -->\n",
    "closed_at": "2019-11-20T04:54:25Z",
